; The one zone on this bench that points at something which ANSWERS.
;
; EVERY OTHER NAME HERE RESOLVES INTO A DOCUMENTATION RANGE ON PURPOSE, so that
; a run against the DNS bench cannot accidentally open a connection to anything.
; This zone is the deliberate exception: scenarios S-1 and S-5 are about what a
; server PRESENTS during a handshake, and there is no way to ask that question of
; an address nobody listens on.
;
; The address is inside the bench's own subnet and is unreachable from anywhere
; else, so the exception does not widen past this compose file.
$ORIGIN partner.test.
$TTL 60

@   IN SOA ns.partner.test. admin.partner.test. (
        1          ; serial
        7200       ; refresh
        3600       ; retry
        1209600    ; expire
        3600 )     ; minimum

@   IN NS  ns.partner.test.
ns  IN A   172.28.0.53

; The server holding a leaf whose intermediate it never sends - S-5.
@   IN A   172.28.0.80
